Package: exposomeSC
Title: Single-Cell Exposome-Wide Association Studies
    with Cross-Omic Network Inference
Version: 0.99.0
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Cuiwei",
           family = "Gao",
           email = "48gaocuiwei@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A framework for cell-type-specific exposome-wide
    association studies (sc-ExWAS) that bridges donor-level
    environmental exposures with single-cell resolution gene
    expression. The package extends SingleCellExperiment to
    store exposure measurements alongside transcriptomic data,
    and implements donor-level raw-count pseudobulk inference to
    avoid cellular pseudoreplication (Squair et al. 2021
    <doi:10.1038/s41467-021-25960-2>). The default workflow uses
    robust edgeR quasi-likelihood models, exposure-independent
    expression-support filtering, complete-transcriptome offsets,
    design-rank diagnostics, and global multiplicity correction.
    Additional modules support repeated-sample sensitivity analyses,
    dose-response modelling, exposure mixtures, cross-cohort
    synthesis, and cell-level gene-protein coupling. Exploratory
    decomposition and mediation utilities report model-based
    associations; they do not by themselves identify causal effects.
